    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T04:05:50Z",
    "body": "Findings from the public Sodick LN1W / LN2W training manual (part number 6300015, 2012):\n\n- The manual confirms C001 for the first cut, C002 for the second cut and C903 for the third cut.\n- Its program example selects the next pass's C word after the pass returns to its start point, with the wire threaded. PR #2698 writes the skim C words there.\n- The manual names C000 / H000 \"Approach\" in the condition header, but it shows no program line with C000. PR #2698 makes C000 an option (`approachCondition`, default off). The option cuts the first approach move on C000.\n\nNot confirmed, and the owner must check at a control:\n\n- the placement of C000, and if it is used at each start hole;\n- the flushing for skim passes (follow-up #2686).\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
